# Two git installations share this working tree: Git for Windows on Jarrod's
# machine and the Linux git this session runs. Windows git checks out CRLF by
# default, the Linux one does not, so every file showed as modified after a
# pull and one careless `git add -A` would have committed a whole-repo
# whitespace diff. Pinning to LF makes both agree; the index is already LF, so
# this changes nothing that is committed.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.zip  binary
